hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"159","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) lifted the curtain of his chamber (and saw that) the people were praying behind Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). He (ﷺ) said: ""Beware! I have been forbidden from reciting the Qur'an in bowing and prostration. In bowing, glorify the greatness of your Lord « سُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الْعَظِيمِ » and in prostration, make abundant supplication, for this is the state in which supplications are most likely to be accepted."""
"160","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade wearing silk clothing, yellow-colored clothing, wearing a gold ring, and reciting the Qur'an during bowing (ruku‘)."
"161","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade me—I do not say that He forbade you—from reciting the Qur'an in bowing or prostration, or from wearing a gold ring."
"162","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the Imam says Ameen, you should also say Ameen, because the angels also say Ameen. Whoever's Ameen coincides with the Ameen of the angels, his previous sins are forgiven."""
"163","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the Imam says Ameen, you should also say Ameen. Indeed, whoever's Ameen coincides with the Ameen of the angels, all his past sins are forgiven."""
"164","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When the Imam says ﴿غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ﴾ , you should all say Ameen; whoever's saying coincides with that of the angels, his sins will be forgiven."""
"165","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When one of you says Ameen, the angels in the heavens also say Ameen. So when the Ameen on earth coincides with the Ameen in the heavens, sins are forgiven."""
"166","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the Imam says « سَمِعَ اللهُ لِمَنْ حَمِدَهُ » , you should say « اللهمَّ رَبَّنَا لَكَ الْحَمْدُ » ; for whoever's 'Ameen' coincides with the 'Ameen' of the angels, his sins are forgiven."""
